 :defects-found-during-closure
 ["su-exec exits 1 when it cannot exec, erasing the 127 that distinguishes a missing command from one that ran and failed; the drop now goes through a shell"
  "su-exec resets HOME from a passwd file the derived uid does not appear in, leaving HOME on a filesystem the workload cannot write; HOME is set after the drop"
  "busybox setpriv cannot change uid, and installing util-linux to get one introduces a setuid mount that setuid-stripping then deletes; su-exec avoids both"
  "a renamed gate key (:version/tool-bundle-required -> :version/guest-image-required) was not updated in script/build-native and stopped a build"
  "the A3a phases printed namespace-abbreviated maps on the JVM and full keys in the image, so their gate patterns could not be verified outside a build; all phases now share one emitter"
  "the live dogfood harness hardcoded its output path and overwrote A3b's dogfood record with A3c-era results; the path is now an argument and A3b's record was restored"]

 :nonclaims
 ["the machine is still the hard host-isolation boundary; A3c is defence in depth behind it and does not replace the hypervisor"
  "this is proof against umount, not against a kernel bug"
  "the guest image is trusted, not verified; its digest says which bytes ran, not that they are benign"
  "the overlay's lower layer is still live; a moved project is still reported as :project-changed rather than prevented"
  "a root-owned project is refused, not handled"
  "A3b's records describe a root workload and are accurate for A3b; they were annotated, not rewritten"]

